SharedHandle extension: export textures and fences to other APIs and processes.

NRI has no way to export a texture's memory or a fence: TextureDesc and AllocateMemoryDesc carry no
exportable flag, CreateFence takes no desc, and the Vulkan backend loads one external-memory entry
point for its own use only. A compositor or editor that imports a renderer's output needs exactly
that.

This patch adds one NRI-shaped extension, NRISharedHandle.h:

  - SharedHandleType, SharedHandle
  - SharedHandleInterface::CreateSharedTexture   committed, dedicated, exportable (VK: VkExternalMemoryImageCreateInfo + VkExportMemoryAllocateInfo, not through VMA; D3D12: D3D12_HEAP_FLAG_SHARED)
  - SharedHandleInterface::CreateSharedFence     timeline fence that can be exported (VK: VkExportSemaphoreCreateInfo; D3D12: D3D12_FENCE_FLAG_SHARED);
                                                 with the SWAPCHAIN_SEMAPHORE initial value an exportable binary semaphore (VK only,
                                                 UNSUPPORTED on D3D12), the signal-once/wait-once object external compositors import
  - SharedHandleInterface::GetTextureSharedHandle / GetFenceSharedHandle   a new caller-owned handle per call (VK: vkGetMemory*/vkGetSemaphore* Win32HandleKHR or FdKHR; D3D12: ID3D12Device::CreateSharedHandle)
  - EXTERNAL_QUEUE                               a sentinel for TextureBarrierDesc::srcQueue / dstQueue: VK writes VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_EXTERNAL
                                                 for it, also on CONCURRENT images where every other side is IGNORED; validation passes
                                                 it through; D3D12's copy-queue check skips it

The Vulkan backend enables VK_KHR_external_memory_win32/fd and VK_KHR_external_semaphore_win32/fd
when the device has them (skipping any the app already requested through vkExtensions) and reports
the extension UNSUPPORTED when it does not. CreateSharedTexture records the image's sharing mode as
TextureVK::Create does, so barriers on a CONCURRENT shared texture carry no queue family indices.
The NONE backend returns dummy objects and a zero handle. The validation layer wraps the four
calls.

Applies on top of NRI main 2f7a49f and patch 0001. Re-cut on 2026-10-21 over 2603edc (#284) and
732f737 (#283), which left three of its spots stale: the barrier's queue family lines, the
concurrency flag of its own create path, and D3D12's copy-queue check, which would otherwise read a
QueueD3D12 at address 1.

